# affect_join: an affect that stacks on one of the same type. Glutton (10, never too full to drink) drinks two
# poisoned herbal brews (1351) in the temple (3001): the second poison joins the first, and @state shows one
# poison affect, with the durations and modifiers added and the levels averaged. affect_join averaged them with
# paf->level = (paf->level += paf_old->level) / 2, which writes paf->level twice in one expression: undefined
# behaviour, which gcc warns about (#14). The fix adds the levels without writing to paf->level first.
@connect glut
Glutton
psswrd
@return
@obj 1351 3001
@obj 1351 3001
get all.brew
drink brew
@state
drink 2.brew
@state
